1.26.0: make install, man pages, assets found from anywhere

Install:
- 'make install' puts polajuice, superjuice and super8ify in ~/.local/bin,
  the print stocks and the workspace page in ~/.local/share/polajuice/,
  the man pages in ~/.local/share/man/man1/, and fills
  ~/.local/share/polajuice/luts with the film library (a library already
  in the source tree is copied, the rest downloaded). 'make install-files'
  does the same without the network, 'make uninstall' removes everything,
  PREFIX= relocates (PREFIX=/usr/local for a system-wide install),
  'make install-dev' adds the header and static library.

Assets:
- the film library, print stocks and web page are found in order: their
  own variable ($POLAJUICE_FILMS/_PRINTS/_WEB), $POLAJUICE_HOME/<name>,
  the source tree relative to the working directory, ~/.local/share/
  polajuice (XDG_DATA_HOME), then the datadir baked in at build time.
  'polajuice paths' prints the result. 'polajuice serve' takes its page
  from the same lookup (--web still overrides).

Docs:
- man pages: polajuice(1), superjuice(1), super8ify(1) in docs/man/.
- 'polajuice --help' now lists the lens and framing flags and --filter.
- README: build and install section.

Tests:
- scripts/test_install.sh (in 'make check'): installs into a scratch
  prefix, runs the installed binaries from an unrelated directory
  against assets found through XDG_DATA_HOME and $POLAJUICE_HOME, serves
  the installed page, and checks that uninstall leaves nothing.
